1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,660
One in five hundred people has this disease.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:08,890
A test catches ninety-nine percent of cases and wrongly flags one percent of the healthy.

3
00:00:09,270 --> 00:00:12,240
If yours says positive, what's the chance you're sick?

4
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:13,510
Pick a number.

5
00:00:15,466 --> 00:00:18,536
Most doctors given a problem like this got it wrong.

6
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:24,860
The tempting answer is the test's own hit rate, ninety-nine percent: you'd start treatment today.

7
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,930
Check that rule by counting.

8
00:00:27,130 --> 00:00:30,960
Here are ten thousand people, and suppose half of them are sick.

9
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:32,430
Test everyone.

10
00:00:32,630 --> 00:00:36,860
Ninety-nine percent of the sick light up, and one percent of the healthy.

11
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:41,020
Of the five thousand who lit up, ninety-nine percent are sick.

12
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:42,800
Here, the rule holds.

13
00:00:43,166 --> 00:00:47,166
Now make the disease rare, like yours: one in five hundred.

14
00:00:47,366 --> 00:00:49,276
That leaves twenty sick people.

15
00:00:49,633 --> 00:00:50,973
Run the same test.

16
00:00:51,173 --> 00:00:57,633
About twenty sick people light up, plus one percent of the nine thousand nine hundred eighty healthy ones.

17
00:00:57,833 --> 00:00:59,283
That's about a hundred.

18
00:00:59,633 --> 00:01:03,383
So of a hundred and twenty positives, only twenty are sick.

19
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:05,400
That's seventeen percent.

20
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,130
The rule said ninety-nine.

21
00:01:08,330 --> 00:01:09,910
Six times too high.

22
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:15,510
One percent sounds small, but here it's one percent of nearly everyone.

23
00:01:15,866 --> 00:01:20,416
Your positive result ruled out everyone who tested negative.

24
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:26,110
What's left is a smaller sample space: these hundred and twenty people.

25
00:01:26,466 --> 00:01:29,826
Your chance of being sick is the red share of this crowd.

26
00:01:30,126 --> 00:01:32,526
Twenty, out of twenty plus a hundred.

27
00:01:34,133 --> 00:01:38,413
Before rounding, these are nineteen point eight and ninety-nine point eight.

28
00:01:38,793 --> 00:01:41,913
That's twenty sick people times ninety-nine percent.

29
00:01:42,293 --> 00:01:46,173
And nine thousand nine hundred eighty healthy times one percent.

30
00:01:46,533 --> 00:01:48,953
Divide top and bottom by ten thousand.

31
00:01:49,153 --> 00:01:58,473
The share stays the same, but each head count becomes a fraction of everyone: two in a thousand, and nine hundred ninety-eight in a thousand.

32
00:01:58,833 --> 00:02:01,103
These two say how common each group is.

33
00:02:01,303 --> 00:02:04,403
These two, how often each group tests positive.

34
00:02:04,703 --> 00:02:06,123
That's Bayes' theorem.

35
00:02:06,466 --> 00:02:11,756
All it does is shrink the sample space to what the evidence allows, then take the share.

36
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:22,780
As for those gynecologists: after one session turning percentages into counts of women, the way we just counted people, eighty-seven percent got it right.

37
00:02:23,133 --> 00:02:25,613
Swap the disease for a police watch list.

38
00:02:25,966 --> 00:02:32,786
At the twenty seventeen Champions League final, about a hundred and seventy thousand people were in Cardiff.

39
00:02:32,986 --> 00:02:40,536
The watch lists held about twelve hundred faces, so even a small error rate per face would swamp the real matches.

40
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:47,290
Face-recognition cameras scanned the crowd and raised two thousand four hundred and seventy alerts.

41
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:52,210
Police counted a hundred and seventy-three as right: seven percent.

42
00:02:52,566 --> 00:02:56,916
In machine learning, the share of alerts that are right is called precision.

43
00:02:57,266 --> 00:03:04,846
Later, a new algorithm and better photos cut the false alarms, and forty-six percent of alerts were judged right.

44
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:06,420
Back to your test.

45
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:10,560
The title's ninety-nine percent accuracy is real.

46
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:17,260
But a test that calls everyone healthy scores ninety-nine point eight: more accurate, and useless.

47
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:20,830
Your seventeen percent assumes a random screen.

48
00:03:21,130 --> 00:03:31,230
Symptoms raise the one in five hundred, and the answer climbs: fifty percent at one in a hundred, ninety-nine at one in two, where the rule held.

49
00:03:32,230 --> 00:03:37,560
On a random screen, twenty reach this plus along the red, a hundred along the blue.

50
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:43,010
Ninety-nine percent is the test's recall: how often the sick test positive.

51
00:03:43,310 --> 00:03:48,130
Seventeen percent is its precision: how often the positive are sick.

